لإنشاء تطبيقات ملاحظات متعددة المنصات"},"features":{"en":["Utilizes GUI design principles for cross-platform compatibility","Follows Rust-specific design principles for efficient development","Performs planning and analysis before code implementation","Reviews existing codebase for conventions and utilities","Identifies platform-specific constraints for targeted GUI work","Considers edge cases within reason for robust application development"],"zh":["跨平台记事本开发","GUI 设计和开发","Notepad++ 功能兼容","平台特定约束处理","边缘情况考虑"],"ja":["AIエージェントの GUI 設計","Rust プログラミング言語","Notepad++ 機能との連携","プラットフォーム特有の制約への対応","エッジケースの考慮"],"ko":["노트패드++ 연동 도구 개발","Rust 프로그래밍 언어","GUI 설계 및 개발","플랫폼 특정 제약 처리","Edge 케이스 고려"],"es":["Interfaz gráfica de usuario inspirada en Notepad++","Desarrollo de aplicaciones de escritorio cross-plataforma","Uso de módulos compartidos y utilidades existentes","Consideración de casos límite y restricciones de plataforma","Diseño de principios específicos de Rust"],"fr":["Interface graphique utilisateur inspirée de Notepad++","Développement d''applications de bureau cross-plateforme","Utilisation de modules partagés et d''utilitaires existants","Prise en compte des cas limites et des contraintes de plateforme","Conception de principes spécifiques à Rust"],"de":["Grafische Benutzeroberfläche, die von Notepad++ inspiriert ist","Erstellung von cross-plattformfähigen Desktop-Anwendungen","Verwendung von gemeinsam genutzten Modulen und vorhandenen Utilities","Berücksichtigung von Randfällen und Plattformbeschränkungen","Entwurf von Rust-spezifischen Prinzipien"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de aplicações de notas cross-plataforma","Inspiração no Notepad++","Utilização de GUI para interfaces de usuário","Compatibilidade com múltiplas plataformas","Análise de requisitos e restrições antes do desenvolvimento","Utilização de módulos compartilhados para reduzir a duplicação de código"],"ru":["Разработка кроссплатформенных приложений для заметок","Вдохновение от Notepad++","Использование GUI для интерфейсов пользователя","Совместимость с несколькими платформами","Анализ требований и ограничений перед разработкой","Использование общих модулей для уменьшения дублирования кода с помощью ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["تطوير تطبيقات ملاحظات متعددة المنصات","الإلهام من Notepad++","استخدام واجهة المستخدم الرسومية","التوافق مع منصات متعددة","تحليل المتطلبات والقيود قبل التطوير","استخدام الوحدات المشتركة لتقليل تكرار الكود"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use rust for notepad","rust alternative to notepad++","rust vs notepad++","rust setup guide for developers","what is rust programming language","rust install for cross-platform development","rust gui development best practices","rust notepad inspired application","rust cross-platform notepad setup"],"zh":["Rust 跨平台开发","GUI 设计","Notepad++ 功能","AIエージェント开发","Rust 编程","跨平台记事本"],"ja":["Rust AIエージェント","GUI 設計","Notepad++ 機能","AIツール開発","Rust プログラミング","クロスプラットフォーム開発"],"ko":["Rust 노트패드++","GUI 설계","Notepad++ 기능","AI 에이전트 개발","Rust 프로그래밍","크로스 플랫폼 개발"],"es":["Rust para desarrolladores","Guía de configuración de Rust","Aplicaciones de escritorio cross-plataforma","Interfaz gráfica de usuario en Rust","Desarrollo de aplicaciones con Rust","Herramientas de desarrollo de Rust"],"fr":["Rust pour les développeurs","Guide de mise en route de Rust","Applications de bureau cross-plateforme","Interface graphique utilisateur en Rust","Développement d''applications avec Rust","Outils de développement de Rust"],"de":["Rust für Entwickler","Rust-Setup-Anleitung","Cross-plattformfähige Desktop-Anwendungen","Grafische Benutzeroberfläche in Rust","Erstellung von Anwendungen mit Rust","Entwicklungstools für Rust"],"pt":["Rust","desenvolvimento de aplicações","notas cross-plataforma","Notepad++","GUI","compatibilidade multiplataforma","análise de requisitos","módulos compartilhados","programação Rust"],"ru":["Rust","разработка приложений","заметки кроссплатформенные","Notepad++","GUI","совместимость мультиплатформенная","анализ требований","общие модули","программирование на Rust","ИИ Агенты"],"ar":["الرست","تطوير التطبيقات","ملاحظات متعددة المنصات","Notepad++","واجهة المستخدم الرسومية","التوافق مع منصات متعددة","تحليل المتطلبات","الوحدات المشتركة","برمجة الرست"]}},"owner":"brenordv","repo":"rust-pad","repoPath":"brenordv/rust-pad","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T06:29:36Z","topics":["gui","notebook","notepad","notepad-plus-plus","notes","tools"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust","description":"Write production-quality Rust code following industry best practices and idiomatic patterns. Use for any Rust coding task including applications, libraries, refactoring, debugging, or code review — with particular expertise in cross-platform GUI development.","bodyPreview":"## Instructions\n\n### 1. Planning & Analysis\n\n**Before writing any code:**\n- Understand the full requirements and constraints\n- Review the existing codebase for conventions, utilities, and patterns already in use\n- Check for shared/common modules before creating new utilities\n- Consider edge cases within reason unless the user specifically asks for more\n- For GUI work: identify which platforms are targeted and any platform-specific constraints\n\n### 2. Design Principles\n\n**Rust-Specific:**\n- Prefe","body":"## Instructions\n\n### 1. Planning & Analysis\n\n**Before writing any code:**\n- Understand the full requirements and constraints\n- Review the existing codebase for conventions, utilities, and patterns already in use\n- Check for shared/common modules before creating new utilities\n- Consider edge cases within reason unless the user specifically asks for more\n- For GUI work: identify which platforms are targeted and any platform-specific constraints\n\n### 2. Design Principles\n\n**Rust-Specific:**\n- Prefer borrowing over cloning; pass `&str` not `&String`, `&Path` not `&PathBuf`, `&[T]` not `&Vec<T>`\n- Use enums, newtypes, and the type system to make illegal states unrepresentable\n- Parse raw input into well-typed structures at the boundary, then pass typed data inward\n- Leverage `impl Into<T>`, `AsRef<T>`, and other conversion traits for ergonomic public APIs\n\n**General:**\n- **YAGNI**: Implement only what is required; add complexity as the need arises\n- **KISS**: Favor simplicity and clarity over cleverness\n- **DRY**: Extract shared logic into common modules or helper functions\n- Follow the repo''s existing conventions over personal preference\n\n### 3. Error Handling (anyhow required)\n\n**Use `anyhow` as the primary error-handling crate.** Do not introduce `thiserror`, `eyre`, or other error libraries unless explicitly approved.\n\n- All fallible functions return `anyhow::Result<T>`\n- Attach context at every level with `.context(\"message\")` or `.with_context(|| format!(...))`\n- Propagate errors with `?`; never use `unwrap()` or `expect()` outside test code\n- Use `anyhow::anyhow!(\"message\")` or `anyhow::bail!(\"message\")` for ad-hoc errors\n- At the entrypoint: handle errors gracefully — print to `stderr` and exit with appropriate code\n\n### 4. Project Structure\n\nFollow the structure established by the project. For new projects, use idiomatic Rust conventions:\n\n**Workspace projects:**\n- Place crates under a `crates/` directory; list them in root `Cargo.toml` `[workspace.members]`\n- Shared utilities go in a common crate (e.g., `crates/common/` or `crates/shared/`)\n- Each crate has a focused responsibility\n\n**Single-crate projects:**\n- `src/main.rs` — thin entrypoint: init, parse args/config, call into app logic, handle exit\n- `src/lib.rs` — public API surface; re-exports from submodules\n- `src/models.rs` — domain types, config structs, enums\n- `src/app.rs` (or domain-named module) — core logic\n\n**General guidelines:**\n- Keep `main.rs` thin — it orchestrates; logic lives in library code\n- One module per concern; split files when they exceed ~300 lines\n- Additional modules are fine when they keep things tidy and well-scoped\n- `#[derive(Debug, Clone)]` on config/model structs; add `Copy`, `PartialEq`, `Eq` where appropriate\n- Enums for discrete modes/states; `Option<T>` for optional fields\n\n### 5. Cross-Platform GUI Development\n\nWhen building GUI applications, apply these practices:\n\nBefore doing any visual changes, check the `ui-guidelines.md` at the root of the repo for general guidelines and best \npractices for UI/UX development.\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Separate core logic from UI: business logic in a library crate, UI in the binary crate\n- Use a message/command pattern to communicate between UI and logic layers\n- Keep platform-specific code isolated behind trait abstractions or `#[cfg(target_os)]` gates\n- Design for the event loop: avoid blocking the main/UI thread\n\n**Framework guidance (choose based on project needs):**\n- **iced** — Elm-inspired, pure Rust, good for data-driven UIs. Strengths: type-safe message passing, no unsafe, cross-platform. Use `iced::Application` or `iced::Sandbox` traits.\n- **egui / eframe** — immediate-mode, excellent for tools, dashboards, debug UIs. Strengths: very fast iteration, minimal boilerplate, easy embedding. Use `eframe::App` trait.\n- **Tauri** — web-tech frontend with Rust backend. Strengths: small binary size, leverage web ecosystem, strong IPC. Use for apps where web UI is preferred.\n- **Slint** — declarative UI with `.slint` markup language. Strengths: designer-friendly, embedded-capable, good accessibility.\n- **gtk4-rs / relm4** — GTK4 bindings. Strengths: mature widget set, strong Linux integration. Use `relm4` for Elm-style architecture on top of GTK4.\n- **Dioxus** — React-like with RSX syntax. Strengths: familiar to web devs, cross-platform (desktop, web, mobile).\n\n**Cross-platform considerations:**\n- Test on all target platforms early and regularly (Windows, macOS, Linux at minimum)\n- Use `dirs` or `directories` crate for platform-appropriate config/data/cache paths\n- Handle HiDPI/scaling — use logical pixels, not physical pixels\n- Respect platform conventions for keyboard shortcuts (Cmd vs Ctrl), file paths, and native look-and-feel\n- Use `cfg(target_os)` sparingly and only when truly needed; prefer cross-platform abstractions\n- For file dialogs, system notifications, and other OS integration, use `rfd`, `notify-rust`, or similar cross-platform crates\n\n**State management:**\n- Treat application state as a single source of truth; UI renders from state\n- Use message/event enums to describe state transitions\n- Keep state serializable where practical (enables save/restore, undo/redo)\n- For complex state, consider a reducer pattern or `Arc<Mutex<State>>` for thread-safe sharing\n\n**Async and threading in GUI apps:**\n- Never block the UI thread — offload heavy work to background threads or async tasks\n- Use channels (`std::sync::mpsc`, `crossbeam-channel`, `tokio::sync::mpsc`) to send results back to the UI\n- For async runtimes alongside GUI event loops, use the framework''s built-in async support or run `tokio` on a separate thread\n- Debounce expensive operations triggered by rapid UI events (typing, resizing)\n\n### 6. Code Style\n\n- Use the repo''s `rustfmt` and `clippy` configuration; never change them; fix all warnings\n- `snake_case` for functions/variables/modules/files; `PascalCase` for types; `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants\n- Group imports: `crate::`, external crates, `std::`; no glob imports in production code\n- Doc comments (`///`) on all public items with `# Errors` / `# Panics` sections where applicable\n- Comments explain \"why\", not \"what\"; no commented-out code\n- Functions ~50 lines max; extract helpers when they grow\n- `match` over `if let` chains for multiple variants; guard clauses for early returns\n\n### 7. Dependencies\n\n- Check the existing `Cargo.toml` before adding new dependencies\n- Prefer well-maintained, widely used crates (check download counts, recent activity, `unsafe` usage)\n- Pin major versions; use `cargo update` for patch updates\n- Feature-gate optional functionality to keep compile times and binary size down\n- For cross-platform apps, verify that dependencies support all target platforms\n- Dependencies should be always kept up-to-date with the latest stable versions\n\n**Commonly useful crates:**\n- CLI: `clap` (derive), `indicatif` (progress bars)\n- Serialization: `serde` + `serde_json` / `toml` / `ron`\n- Async: `tokio` (only when genuinely needed)\n- Logging: `tracing` or `log` + `env_logger`\n- File I/O: `tempfile` (tests), `walkdir` (traversal)\n- Cross-platform paths: `dirs`, `directories`\n\n### 8. Performance\n\n- Use `BufReader`/`BufWriter` for file I/O\n- Pre-allocate `Vec` capacity when size is known; use `Cow<''_, str>` to avoid unnecessary allocations\n- Use `std::sync::LazyLock` (or `once_cell::sync::Lazy`) for expensive one-time inits like compiled regexes\n- Profile before optimizing — use `cargo flamegraph`, `criterion` for benchmarks\n- For GUI: keep frame budgets in mind (~16ms for 60fps); avoid allocations in hot render paths\n\n### 9. Testing\n\n- Unit tests: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the bottom of each file; `use super::*`\n- File-based tests: `tempfile::tempdir()` for temporary directories\n- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert; use helper functions to build test fixtures\n- Use `assert!(matches!(...))` for enum variant checks\n- Test happy paths, error conditions, and meaningful boundary values\n- Add tests where it makes sense; don''t add them purely for coverage numbers\n- For GUI: test logic and state management independently from rendering; use snapshot/golden tests for UI if the framework supports it\n\n### 10. Forbidden\n\n- `unsafe` code unless explicitly approved by the user\n- `unwrap()` / `expect()` in non-test code\n- Error libraries other than `anyhow` (no `thiserror`, `eyre`, etc.) unless explicitly approved\n- Changing `rustfmt` or `clippy` settings without explicit approval\n- Blocking the UI/main thread in GUI applications\n\n### 11. Quality Validation\n\nRun before completion (adjust package name to match the project):\n```bash\ncargo build -p <package-name>\ncargo clippy -p <package-name> -- -D warnings\ncargo test -p <package-name>\ncargo fmt -p <package-name> -- --check\n```\n\nFor workspace-wide checks:\n```bash\ncargo build --workspace\ncargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings\ncargo test --workspace\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\n```\n\nNever run git commit. Summarize changes to the user alongside any problems and caveats.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing new Rust applications, libraries, or tools\n- Building cross-platform GUI applications in Rust\n- Adding functionality to existing crates\n- Refactoring, debugging, or reviewing Rust code\n- Any Rust task where production-quality, idiomatic code is expected"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-07T03:42:00.011Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Systems Programming Agents needing memory-safe and cross-platform development capabilities with Rust.","zh":"非常适合需要内存安全和跨平台开发能力的系统编程代理，使用Rust。","ja":"Rustを使用するシステムプログラミングエージェントに最適です。メモリセーフでクロスプラットフォーム開発が可能です。","ko":"메모리 안전 및 크로스 플랫폼 개발 기능이 필요한 시스템 프로그래밍 에이전트에게 적합한 솔루션입니다. Rust를 사용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de programación de sistemas que necesitan capacidades de desarrollo seguro en memoria y multiplataforma con Rust.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de programmation système nécessitant des capacités de développement sécurisées en mémoire et multiplateforme avec Rust.","de":"Perfekt für Systemprogrammierungsagenten, die sichereren Speicher und plattformübergreifende Entwicklungsfähigkeiten mit Rust benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Programação de Sistemas que precisam de capacidades de desenvolvimento seguras contra erros de memória e multiplataforma com Rust.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов системного программирования, которым необходимы возможности безопасного и кроссплатформенного разработки с помощью Rust.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات برمجة الأنظمة التي تحتاج إلى قدرات تطوير آمنة ومulti-منصة مع Rust."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build efficient and scalable applications using Rust''s ownership model and borrow checker, with support for cross-platform development and a unified note-taking experience across platforms.","zh":"赋予代理构建高效且可扩展的应用程序的能力，使用Rust的所有权模型和借用检查器，并支持跨平台开发和统一的笔记记录体验。","ja":"Rustの所有権モデルと借用チェッカーを使用して、エージェントが効率的でスケーラブルなアプリケーションを構築できるようにします。クロスプラットフォーム開発と統一的なノートテイキング体験もサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 Rust의 소유권 모델과 빌림 검사기를 사용하여 효율적이고 확장 가능한 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있도록 합니다. 크로스 플랫폼 개발 및统一 노트 기록 경험도 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear aplicaciones eficientes y escalables utilizando el modelo de propiedad y el verificador de préstamos de Rust, con soporte para el desarrollo multiplataforma y una experiencia unificada de toma de notas en todas las plataformas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des applications efficaces et évolutives en utilisant le modèle de propriété et le vérificateur d''emprunt de Rust, avec une prise en charge du développement multiplateforme et une expérience de prise de notes unifiée sur toutes les plateformes.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, effiziente und skalierbare Anwendungen mit Rusts Eigentumsmodell und Überprüfer für Entlehnungen zu erstellen, mit Unterstützung für plattformübergreifende Entwicklung und eine einheitliche Notizenerfassung auf allen Plattformen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicações eficientes e escaláveis utilizando o modelo de propriedade e o verificador de empréstimo do Rust, com suporte ao desenvolvimento multiplataforma e uma experiência de tomar notas unificada em todas as plataformas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать эффективные и масштабируемые приложения, используя модель владения и заемщик Rust, с поддержкой кроссплатформенной разработки и унифицированным опытом ведения заметок на всех платформах.","ar":"يتمكن العميل من بناء تطبيقات فعالة ومتوسعة باستخدام نموذج ملكية Rust ومدقق الإقراض، مع دعم التطوير المتعدد المنصات وتجربة ملاحظة موحدة عبر جميع المنصات."},"useCases":{"en":["Building cross-platform note-taking applications","Developing systems programming projects with memory safety","Creating efficient and scalable applications with Rust"],"zh":["构建跨平台的笔记记录应用程序","使用Rust开发系统编程项目，并确保内存安全","使用Rust创建高效且可扩展的应用程序"],"ja":["クロスプラットフォームのノートテイキングアプリケーションを構築する","Rustを使用してシステムプログラミングプロジェクトを開発し、メモリセーフを実現する","Rustを使用して効率的でスケーラブルなアプリケーションを作成する"],"ko":["크로스 플랫폼 노트 기록 애플리케이션 구축","Rust를 사용하여 시스템 프로그래밍 프로젝트 개발 및 메모리 안전 구현","Rust를 사용하여 효율적이고 확장 가능한 애플리케이션 생성"],"es":["Construir aplicaciones de toma de notas multiplataforma","Desarrollar proyectos de programación de sistemas con seguridad de memoria","Crear aplicaciones eficientes y escalables con Rust"],"fr":["Créer des applications de prise de notes multiplateformes","Développer des projets de programmation système avec sécurité de la mémoire","Créer des applications efficaces et évolutives avec Rust"],"de":["Erstellen von plattformübergreifenden Notizanwendungen","Entwicklung von Systemprogrammierungsprojekten mit Speichersicherheit","Erstellen von effizienten und skalierbaren Anwendungen mit Rust"],"pt":["Construir aplicações de tomar notas multiplataforma","Desenvolver projetos de programação de sistemas com segurança de memória","Criar aplicações eficientes e escaláveis com Rust"],"ru":["Построение кроссплатформенных приложений для заметок","Разработка проектов системного программирования с безопасностью памяти","Создание эффективных и масштабируемых приложений с помощью Rust"],"ar":["بناء تطبيقات ملاحظة متعددة المنصات","تطوير مشاريع برمجة أنظمة مع أمان الذاكرة","إنشاء تطبيقات فعالة ومتوسعة مع Rust"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust compiler and dependencies","Limited to Rust-specific development and note-taking use cases"],"zh":["需要Rust编译器和依赖项","仅限Rust特定开发和笔记记录用例"],"ja":["Rustコンパイラと依存関係が必要","Rust特有の開発とノートテイキング用途のみ"],"ko":["Rust 컴파일러 및 종속 항목이 필요","Rust 특정 개발 및 노트 기록 사용 사례에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere compilador de Rust y dependencias","Limitado a casos de uso de desarrollo y toma de notas específicos de Rust"],"fr":["Nécessite un compilateur Rust et des dépendances","Limité à des cas d''utilisation de développement et de prise de notes spécifiques à Rust"],"de":["Benötigt Rust-Compiler und Abhängigkeiten","Begrenzt auf Rust-spezifische Entwicklungsfälle und Notizenerfassung"],"pt":["Requer compilador Rust e dependências","Limitado a casos de uso de desenvolvimento e tomar notas específicos do Rust"],"ru":["Требуется компилятор Rust и зависимости","Ограничен случаи использования разработки и заметок, специфичные для Rust"],"ar":["يتطلب مترجم Rust والاعتماديات","محدود لحالات استخدام التطوير والتدوين الخاصة بالرست"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"41978aba0c2aee8024cd61d0e035bc0f4ff7f661a0f966772d154428608b04cb","qualityScore":60}');
