e prueba para shell","mejores prácticas para testing de shell"],"fr":["tests unitaires pour shell","Bats Testing Patterns","TDD pour les scripts","tests automatisés dans les pipelines de CI/CD","modèles de test pour les scripts shell","meilleures pratiques pour les tests de shell"],"de":["Einheitstests für Shell-Skripte","Bats-Testing-Patterns","TDD für Skripte","automatisierte Tests in CI/CD-Pipelines","Testmuster für Shell-Skripte","Best Practices für Shell-Testing"],"pt":["bats testing patterns","testes unitários para scripts de shell","padrões de teste para shell","tdd para scripts","testes automatizados em ci/cd","bats para desenvolvedores","testes de produção para shell","melhores práticas para testes de shell"],"ru":["шаблоны тестирования bats","юнит-тесты для скриптов shell","тестовые шаблоны для shell","tdd для скриптов","автоматизированное тестирование в ci/cd","bats для разработчиков","тестирование производственных скриптов","лучшие практики для тестирования shell"],"ar":["أنماط الاختبار bats","اختبارات الوحدوية للبرامج النصية","أنماط الاختبار للبرامج النصية","تطوير قائم على الاختبار (tdd) للبرامج النصية","اختبارات آلية في خطوط أنابيب ci/cd","نظام الاختبار الآلي bats للبرمجة","اختبارات الإنتاج للبرامج النصية","أفضل الممارسات لاختبارات البرامج النصية"]}},"owner":"synqing","repo":"K1.node1","repoPath":"synqing/K1.node1","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-01-08T12:59:54Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bats-testing-patterns","description":"Master Bash Automated Testing System (Bats) for comprehensive shell script testing. Use when writing tests for shell scripts, CI/CD pipelines, or requiring test-driven development of shell utilities.","bodyPreview":"# Bats Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive guidance for writing comprehensive unit tests for shell scripts using Bats (Bash Automated Testing System), including test patterns, fixtures, and best practices for production-grade shell testing.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing unit tests for shell scripts\n- Implementing test-driven development (TDD) for scripts\n- Setting up automated testing in CI/CD pipelines\n- Testing edge cases and error conditions\n- Validating behavior across different shell en","body":"# Bats Testing Patterns\n\nComprehensive guidance for writing comprehensive unit tests for shell scripts using Bats (Bash Automated Testing System), including test patterns, fixtures, and best practices for production-grade shell testing.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Writing unit tests for shell scripts\n- Implementing test-driven development (TDD) for scripts\n- Setting up automated testing in CI/CD pipelines\n- Testing edge cases and error conditions\n- Validating behavior across different shell environments\n- Building maintainable test suites for scripts\n- Creating fixtures for complex test scenarios\n- Testing multiple shell dialects (bash, sh, dash)\n\n## Bats Fundamentals\n\n### What is Bats?\n\nBats (Bash Automated Testing System) is a TAP (Test Anything Protocol) compliant testing framework for shell scripts that provides:\n- Simple, natural test syntax\n- TAP output format compatible with CI systems\n- Fixtures and setup/teardown support\n- Assertion helpers\n- Parallel test execution\n\n### Installation\n\n```bash\n# macOS with Homebrew\nbrew install bats-core\n\n# Ubuntu/Debian\ngit clone https://github.com/bats-core/bats-core.git\ncd bats-core\n./install.sh /usr/local\n\n# From npm (Node.js)\nnpm install --global bats\n\n# Verify installation\nbats --version\n```\n\n### File Structure\n\n```\nproject/\n├── bin/\n│   ├── script.sh\n│   └── helper.sh\n├── tests/\n│   ├── test_script.bats\n│   ├── test_helper.sh\n│   ├── fixtures/\n│   │   ├── input.txt\n│   │   └── expected_output.txt\n│   └── helpers/\n│       └── mocks.bash\n└── README.md\n```\n\n## Basic Test Structure\n\n### Simple Test File\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n# Load test helper if present\nload test_helper\n\n# Setup runs before each test\nsetup() {\n    export TMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)\n}\n\n# Teardown runs after each test\nteardown() {\n    rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"\n}\n\n# Test: simple assertion\n@test \"Function returns 0 on success\" {\n    run my_function \"input\"\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n}\n\n# Test: output verification\n@test \"Function outputs correct result\" {\n    run my_function \"test\"\n    [ \"$output\" = \"expected output\" ]\n}\n\n# Test: error handling\n@test \"Function returns 1 on missing argument\" {\n    run my_function\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 1 ]\n}\n```\n\n## Assertion Patterns\n\n### Exit Code Assertions\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"Command succeeds\" {\n    run true\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n}\n\n@test \"Command fails as expected\" {\n    run false\n    [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]\n}\n\n@test \"Command returns specific exit code\" {\n    run my_function --invalid\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 127 ]\n}\n\n@test \"Can capture command result\" {\n    run echo \"hello\"\n    [ $status -eq 0 ]\n    [ \"$output\" = \"hello\" ]\n}\n```\n\n### Output Assertions\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"Output matches string\" {\n    result=$(echo \"hello world\")\n    [ \"$result\" = \"hello world\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"Output contains substring\" {\n    result=$(echo \"hello world\")\n    [[ \"$result\" == *\"world\"* ]]\n}\n\n@test \"Output matches pattern\" {\n    result=$(date +%Y)\n    [[ \"$result\" =~ ^[0-9]{4}$ ]]\n}\n\n@test \"Multi-line output\" {\n    run printf \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\"\n    [ \"$output\" = \"line1\nline2\nline3\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"Lines variable contains output\" {\n    run printf \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\"\n    [ \"${lines[0]}\" = \"line1\" ]\n    [ \"${lines[1]}\" = \"line2\" ]\n    [ \"${lines[2]}\" = \"line3\" ]\n}\n```\n\n### File Assertions\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"File is created\" {\n    [ ! -f \"$TMPDIR/output.txt\" ]\n    my_function > \"$TMPDIR/output.txt\"\n    [ -f \"$TMPDIR/output.txt\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"File contents match expected\" {\n    my_function > \"$TMPDIR/output.txt\"\n    [ \"$(cat \"$TMPDIR/output.txt\")\" = \"expected content\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"File is readable\" {\n    touch \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\"\n    [ -r \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"File has correct permissions\" {\n    touch \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\"\n    chmod 644 \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\"\n    [ \"$(stat -f %OLp \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\")\" = \"644\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"File size is correct\" {\n    echo -n \"12345\" > \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\"\n    [ \"$(wc -c < \"$TMPDIR/test.txt\")\" -eq 5 ]\n}\n```\n\n## Setup and Teardown Patterns\n\n### Basic Setup and Teardown\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\nsetup() {\n    # Create test directory\n    TEST_DIR=$(mktemp -d)\n    export TEST_DIR\n\n    # Source script under test\n    source \"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME}/../bin/script.sh\"\n}\n\nteardown() {\n    # Clean up temporary directory\n    rm -rf \"$TEST_DIR\"\n}\n\n@test \"Test using TEST_DIR\" {\n    touch \"$TEST_DIR/file.txt\"\n    [ -f \"$TEST_DIR/file.txt\" ]\n}\n```\n\n### Setup with Resources\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\nsetup() {\n    # Create directory structure\n    mkdir -p \"$TMPDIR/data/input\"\n    mkdir -p \"$TMPDIR/data/output\"\n\n    # Create test fixtures\n    echo \"line1\" > \"$TMPDIR/data/input/file1.txt\"\n    echo \"line2\" > \"$TMPDIR/data/input/file2.txt\"\n\n    # Initialize environment\n    export DATA_DIR=\"$TMPDIR/data\"\n    export INPUT_DIR=\"$DATA_DIR/input\"\n    export OUTPUT_DIR=\"$DATA_DIR/output\"\n}\n\nteardown() {\n    rm -rf \"$TMPDIR/data\"\n}\n\n@test \"Processes input files\" {\n    run my_process_script \"$INPUT_DIR\" \"$OUTPUT_DIR\"\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n    [ -f \"$OUTPUT_DIR/file1.txt\" ]\n}\n```\n\n### Global Setup/Teardown\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n# Load shared setup from test_helper.sh\nload test_helper\n\n# setup_file runs once before all tests\nsetup_file() {\n    export SHARED_RESOURCE=$(mktemp -d)\n    echo \"Expensive setup\" > \"$SHARED_RESOURCE/data.txt\"\n}\n\n# teardown_file runs once after all tests\nteardown_file() {\n    rm -rf \"$SHARED_RESOURCE\"\n}\n\n@test \"First test uses shared resource\" {\n    [ -f \"$SHARED_RESOURCE/data.txt\" ]\n}\n\n@test \"Second test uses shared resource\" {\n    [ -d \"$SHARED_RESOURCE\" ]\n}\n```\n\n## Mocking and Stubbing Patterns\n\n### Function Mocking\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n# Mock external command\nmy_external_tool() {\n    echo \"mocked output\"\n    return 0\n}\n\n@test \"Function uses mocked tool\" {\n    export -f my_external_tool\n    run my_function\n    [[ \"$output\" == *\"mocked output\"* ]]\n}\n```\n\n### Command Stubbing\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\nsetup() {\n    # Create stub directory\n    STUBS_DIR=\"$TMPDIR/stubs\"\n    mkdir -p \"$STUBS_DIR\"\n\n    # Add to PATH\n    export PATH=\"$STUBS_DIR:$PATH\"\n}\n\ncreate_stub() {\n    local cmd=\"$1\"\n    local output=\"$2\"\n    local code=\"${3:-0}\"\n\n    cat > \"$STUBS_DIR/$cmd\" <<EOF\n#!/bin/bash\necho \"$output\"\nexit $code\nEOF\n    chmod +x \"$STUBS_DIR/$cmd\"\n}\n\n@test \"Function works with stubbed curl\" {\n    create_stub curl \"{ \\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\" }\" 0\n    run my_api_function\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n}\n```\n\n### Variable Stubbing\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"Function handles environment override\" {\n    export MY_SETTING=\"override_value\"\n    run my_function\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n    [[ \"$output\" == *\"override_value\"* ]]\n}\n\n@test \"Function uses default when var unset\" {\n    unset MY_SETTING\n    run my_function\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n    [[ \"$output\" == *\"default\"* ]]\n}\n```\n\n## Fixture Management\n\n### Using Fixture Files\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n# Fixture directory: tests/fixtures/\n\nsetup() {\n    FIXTURES_DIR=\"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME}/fixtures\"\n    WORK_DIR=$(mktemp -d)\n    export WORK_DIR\n}\n\nteardown() {\n    rm -rf \"$WORK_DIR\"\n}\n\n@test \"Process fixture file\" {\n    # Copy fixture to work directory\n    cp \"$FIXTURES_DIR/input.txt\" \"$WORK_DIR/input.txt\"\n\n    # Run function\n    run my_process_function \"$WORK_DIR/input.txt\"\n\n    # Compare output\n    diff \"$WORK_DIR/output.txt\" \"$FIXTURES_DIR/expected_output.txt\"\n}\n```\n\n### Dynamic Fixture Generation\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\ngenerate_fixture() {\n    local lines=\"$1\"\n    local file=\"$2\"\n\n    for i in $(seq 1 \"$lines\"); do\n        echo \"Line $i content\" >> \"$file\"\n    done\n}\n\n@test \"Handle large input file\" {\n    generate_fixture 1000 \"$TMPDIR/large.txt\"\n    run my_function \"$TMPDIR/large.txt\"\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n    [ \"$(wc -l < \"$TMPDIR/large.txt\")\" -eq 1000 ]\n}\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Testing Error Conditions\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"Function fails with missing file\" {\n    run my_function \"/nonexistent/file.txt\"\n    [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]\n    [[ \"$output\" == *\"not found\"* ]]\n}\n\n@test \"Function fails with invalid input\" {\n    run my_function \"\"\n    [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]\n}\n\n@test \"Function fails with permission denied\" {\n    touch \"$TMPDIR/readonly.txt\"\n    chmod 000 \"$TMPDIR/readonly.txt\"\n    run my_function \"$TMPDIR/readonly.txt\"\n    [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]\n    chmod 644 \"$TMPDIR/readonly.txt\"  # Cleanup\n}\n\n@test \"Function provides helpful error message\" {\n    run my_function --invalid-option\n    [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]\n    [[ \"$output\" == *\"Usage:\"* ]]\n}\n```\n\n### Testing with Dependencies\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\nsetup() {\n    # Check for required tools\n    if ! command -v jq &>/dev/null; then\n        skip \"jq is not installed\"\n    fi\n\n    export SCRIPT=\"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME}/../bin/script.sh\"\n}\n\n@test \"JSON parsing works\" {\n    skip_if ! command -v jq &>/dev/null\n    run my_json_parser ''{\"key\": \"value\"}''\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n}\n```\n\n### Testing Shell Compatibility\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"Script works in bash\" {\n    bash \"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME}/../bin/script.sh\" arg1\n}\n\n@test \"Script works in sh (POSIX)\" {\n    sh \"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME}/../bin/script.sh\" arg1\n}\n\n@test \"Script works in dash\" {\n    if command -v dash &>/dev/null; then\n        dash \"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME}/../bin/script.sh\" arg1\n    else\n        skip \"dash not installed\"\n    fi\n}\n```\n\n### Parallel Execution\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bats\n\n@test \"Multiple independent operations\" {\n    run bash -c ''for i in {1..10}; do\n        my_operation \"$i\" &\n    done\n    wait''\n    [ \"$status\" -eq 0 ]\n}\n\n@test \"Concurrent file operations\" {\n    for i in {1..5}; do\n        my_function \"$TMPDIR/file$i\" &\n    done\n    wait\n    [ -f \"$TMPDIR/file1\" ]\n    [ -f \"$TMPDIR/file5\" ]\n}\n```\n\n## Test Helper Pattern\n\n### test_helper.sh\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n\n# Source script under test\nexport SCRIPT_DIR=\"${BATS_TEST_DIRNAME%/*}/bin\"\n\n# Common test utilities\nassert_file_exists() {\n    if [ ! -f \"$1\" ]; then\n        echo \"Expected file to exist: $1\"\n        return 1\n    fi\n}\n\nassert_file_equals() {\n    local file=\"$1\"\n    local expected=\"$2\"\n\n    if [ ! -f \"$file\" ]; then\n        echo \"File does not exist: $file\"\n        return 1\n    fi\n\n    local actual=$(cat \"$file\")\n    if [ \"$actual\" != \"$expected\" ]; then\n        echo \"File contents do not match\"\n        echo \"Expected: $expected\"\n        echo \"Actual: $actual\"\n        return 1\n    fi\n}\n\n# Create temporary test directory\nsetup_test_dir() {\n    export TEST_DIR=$(mktemp -d)\n}\n\ncleanup_test_dir() {\n    rm -rf \"$TEST_DIR\"\n}\n```\n\n## Integration with CI/CD\n\n### GitHub Actions Workflow\n\n```yaml\nname: Tests\n\non: [push, pull_request]\n\njobs:\n  test:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n\n      - name: Install Bats\n        run: |\n          npm install --global bats\n\n      - name: Run Tests\n        run: |\n          bats tests/*.bats\n\n      - name: Run Tests with Tap Reporter\n        run: |\n          bats tests/*.bats --tap | tee test_output.tap\n```\n\n### Makefile Integration\n\n```makefile\n.PHONY: test test-verbose test-tap\n\ntest:\n\tbats tests/*.bats\n\ntest-verbose:\n\tbats tests/*.bats --verbose\n\ntest-tap:\n\tbats tests/*.bats --tap\n\ntest-parallel:\n\tbats tests/*.bats --parallel 4\n\ncoverage: test\n\t# Optional: Generate coverage reports\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Test one thing per test** - Single responsibility principle\n2. **Use descriptive test names** - Clearly states what is being tested\n3. **Clean up after tests** - Always remove temporary files in teardown\n4. **Test both success and failure paths** - Don''t just test happy path\n5. **Mock external dependencies** - Isolate unit under test\n6. **Use fixtures for complex data** - Makes tests more readable\n7. **Run tests in CI/CD** - Catch regressions early\n8. **Test across shell dialects** - Ensure portability\n9. **Keep tests fast** - Run in parallel when possible\n10. **Document complex test setup** - Explain unusual patterns\n\n## Resources\n\n- **Bats GitHub**: https://github.com/bats-core/bats-core\n- **Bats Documentation**: https://bats-core.readthedocs.io/\n- **TAP Protocol**: https://testanything.org/\n- **Test-Driven Development**: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test-driven_development\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-07T03:48:36.163Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for DevOps Agents needing comprehensive shell script testing capabilities using Bats","zh":"非常适合需要使用Bats进行全面shell脚本测试的DevOps代理","ja":"Batsを使用した包括的なシェルスクリプトテスト機能を必要とするDevOpsエージェントに最適","ko":"Bats를 사용하여 포괄적인 셸 스크립트 테스트 기능이 필요한 DevOps 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de DevOps que necesitan capacidades de prueba de scripts de shell integrales utilizando Bats","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps ayant besoin de capacités de test de scripts shell complets en utilisant Bats","de":"Perfekt für DevOps-Agents, die umfassende Shell-Skript-Testfunktionen mit Bats benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes DevOps que necessitam de capacidades abrangentes de teste de scripts de shell usando Bats","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, которым требуются всесторонние возможности тестирования shell-скриптов с использованием Bats","ar":"مثالي لعميل DevOps الذين يحتاجون إلى khảیات شاملة لاختبار سكريبتات Shell باستخدام Bats"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write unit tests for shell scripts using Bats, including test patterns, fixtures, and best practices for production-grade shell testing, leveraging Bash Automated Testing System for test-driven development and automated testing in CI/CD pipelines","zh":"赋予代理编写使用Bats的shell脚本单元测试的能力，包括测试模式、固定装置和生产级shell测试的最佳实践，利用Bash Automated Testing System进行测试驱动开发和CI/CD管道中的自动化测试","ja":"エージェントがBatsを使用したシェルスクリプトのユニットテストを記述する能力を提供し、テストパターン、フィクスチャ、生产レベルのシェルテストのベストプラクティスを含み、Bash Automated Testing Systemを使用してテスト駆動開発とCI/CDパイプラインでの自動テストを実現する","ko":"에이전트가 Bats를 사용하여 셸 스크립트의 단위 테스트를 작성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 테스트 패턴, 고정 장치 및 생산급 셸 테스트의 모범 사례를 포함하며, Bash Automated Testing System를 사용하여 테스트 주도 개발 및 CI/CD 파이프라인에서의 자동화 테스트를 구현","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas unitarias para scripts de shell utilizando Bats, incluyendo patrones de prueba, fixtures y mejores prácticas para pruebas de shell de nivel de producción, aprovechando el sistema de prueba automatizada de Bash para el desarrollo impulsado por pruebas y pruebas automatizadas en tuberías de CI/CD","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests unitaires pour les scripts shell en utilisant Bats, y compris les modèles de test, les fixtures et les meilleures pratiques pour les tests de shell de production, en exploitant le système de test automatisé Bash pour le développement piloté par les tests et les tests automatisés dans les pipelines de CI/CD","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Unit-Tests für Shell-Skripte mit Bats zu schreiben, einschließlich Testmustern, Fixtures und Best Practices für produktionsreife Shell-Tests, indem es das Bash-Automated-Testing-System für testgetriebene Entwicklung und automatisierte Tests in CI/CD-Pipelines nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever testes unitários para scripts de shell usando Bats, incluindo padrões de teste, fixtures e melhores práticas para testes de shell de produção, aproveitando o Sistema de Teste Automatizado do Bash para desenvolvimento orientado a testes e testes automatizados em pipelines de CI/CD","ru":"Позволяет агентам писать модульные тесты для shell-скриптов с использованием Bats, включая модели тестирования, фикстуры и лучшие практики для производственных тестов shell, используя Автоматизированную Систему Тестирования Bash для разработки, ориентированной на тестирование, и автоматизированного тестирования в конвейерах CI/CD","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية كتابة اختبارات وحدة لسكريبتات Shell باستخدام Bats، بما في ذلك أنماط الاختبار والإعدادات وأفضل الممارسات لاختبارات Shell الإنتاجية، واستخدام نظام اختبار Bash الآلي لتطوير قائم على الاختبار واختبارات آلية في أنابيب CI/CD"},"useCases":{"en":["Writing unit tests for shell scripts","Implementing test-driven development for scripts","Setting up automated testing in CI/CD pipelines","Testing edge cases and error conditions"],"zh":["为shell脚本编写单元测试","为脚本实现测试驱动开发","在CI/CD管道中设置自动化测试","测试边缘情况和错误条件"],"ja":["シェルスクリプトのユニットテストを記述する","スクリプトのテスト駆動開発を実現する","CI/CDパイプラインで自動テストを設定する","エッジケースとエラーコンディションをテストする"],"ko":["셸 스크립트의 단위 테스트를 작성","스크립트의 테스트 주도 개발을 구현","CI/CD 파이프라인에서 자동화 테스트를 설정","에지 케이스와 오류 조건을 테스트"],"es":["Escribir pruebas unitarias para scripts de shell","Implementar desarrollo impulsado por pruebas para scripts","Configurar pruebas automatizadas en tuberías de CI/CD","Probar casos límite y condiciones de error"],"fr":["Écrire des tests unitaires pour les scripts shell","Mettre en œuvre le développement piloté par les tests pour les scripts","Configurer les tests automatisés dans les pipelines de CI/CD","Tester les cas limites et les conditions d''erreur"],"de":["Unit-Tests für Shell-Skripte schreiben","Testgetriebene Entwicklung für Skripte implementieren","Automatisierte Tests in CI/CD-Pipelines einrichten","Testen von Randfällen und Fehlerbedingungen"],"pt":["Escrever testes unitários para scripts de shell","Implementar desenvolvimento orientado a testes para scripts","Configurar testes automatizados em pipelines de CI/CD","Testar casos de bordo e condições de erro"],"ru":["Написание модульных тестов для shell-скриптов","Внедрение разработки, ориентированной на тестирование, для скриптов","Настройка автоматизированного тестирования в конвейерах CI/CD","Тестирование граничных случаев и условий ошибок"],"ar":["كتابة اختبارات وحدة لسكريبتات Shell","تنفيذ تطوير قائم على الاختبار لسكريبتات","تكوين اختبارات آلية في أنابيب CI/CD","اختبار الحالات الحدية وظروف الخطأ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Bats installation","Limited to Bash shell scripts","Needs understanding of shell scripting and testing principles"],"zh":["需要Bats安装","仅限于Bash shell脚本","需要了解shell脚本和测试原则"],"ja":["Batsのインストールが必要","Bashシェルスクリプトのみに限定","シェルスクリプトとテスト原則の理解が必要"],"ko":["Bats 설치가 필요","Bash 셸 스크립트만으로 제한","셸 스크립트와 테스트 원칙에 대한 이해가 필요"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Bats","Limitado a scripts de shell de Bash","Necesita comprensión de los principios de scripting y prueba de shell"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Bats","Limité aux scripts shell de Bash","Nécessite une compréhension des principes de scripting et de test de shell"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von Bats","Begrenzt auf Bash-Shell-Skripte","Benötigt Verständnis für Shell-Skripting- und Testprinzipien"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Bats","Limitado a scripts de shell do Bash","Necessita de compreensão de princípios de script de shell e testes"],"ru":["Требует установки Bats","Ограничен скриптами shell Bash","Требует понимания принципов shell-скриптов и тестирования"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Bats","محدود بسكريبتات Shell من Bash","يحتاج إلى فهم مبادئ سكريبتات Shell والاختبارات"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"bbf2ab75641bf